Wiffer RAM filesystem

These files were packed into rootfs.tar (ustar) by build.sh, loaded by
Limine as a boot module, and copied into the kernel's RAM filesystem.
Changes here last until the next reboot. The exception is /disk: a FAT32
volume on the virtio disk (build/disk.img), where every change is written
to the disk before the command returns, so it survives a reboot.

Try: ls, cd, pwd, cat, mkdir, rm, mv, touch, write <file> <text>, df,
and for disks: disks, mount, umount, sync, fsck, mkfs.
